1
00:00:01,793 --> 00:00:05,088
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:14,764
[laughs]

3
00:00:32,782 --> 00:00:34,367
[Salonga] <i>We must study this</i>
<i>more thoroughly</i>

4
00:00:34,451 --> 00:00:38,038
<i>before we get foreign intelligence</i>
<i>involved in Red Dragon's case.</i>

5
00:00:38,121 --> 00:00:40,582
[Lily] <i>I have a spy in</i>
<i>Red Dragon's organization.</i>

6
00:00:40,665 --> 00:00:43,168
<i>We can keep track of their every move.</i>

7
00:00:43,251 --> 00:00:45,712
[Mercedes] <i>Unless I'm certain</i>
<i>of your loyalty, Diego,</i>

8
00:00:45,795 --> 00:00:47,922
<i>I cannot just trust you blindly.</i>

9
00:00:48,006 --> 00:00:51,176
[Lily] <i>I'm worried that</i>
<i>Mercedes has Diego's phone.</i>

10
00:00:51,259 --> 00:00:52,427
[Damian] <i>Maybe I can help.</i>

11
00:00:52,510 --> 00:00:55,388
<i>I used to be in a gang</i>
<i>with Red Dragon's former men.</i>

12
00:00:55,472 --> 00:00:57,557
[Mercedes] <i>We can't do anything to Diego</i>

13
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:59,309
<i>without any solid proof.</i>

14
00:00:59,392 --> 00:01:00,602
[Helena] <i>And while I'm away,</i>

15
00:01:00,685 --> 00:01:03,688
<i>I am entrusting my position</i>
<i>to my baby girl.</i>

16
00:01:03,772 --> 00:01:07,650
<i>My baby dragon, Emilia Ardiente-Torillo.</i>

17
00:01:07,734 --> 00:01:10,570
<i>You are not my queen,</i>
<i>and you will never be.</i>

18
00:01:10,653 --> 00:01:12,781
<i>I'd rather die than kneel before you.</i>

19
00:01:13,573 --> 00:01:16,201
[Emilia] <i>Vanessa, you know</i>
<i>what to do with her.</i>

20
00:01:17,786 --> 00:01:20,371
[Lily] <i>Emilia is born</i>
<i>to lead your faction,</i>

21
00:01:20,455 --> 00:01:22,499
<i>but you are made to rule.</i>

22
00:01:22,582 --> 00:01:25,084
<i>You deserve better,</i>
<i>and you'll get that in my group.</i>

23
00:01:25,168 --> 00:01:29,464
<i>I'd much rather be alone</i>
<i>than become your little pet.</i>

24
00:01:29,547 --> 00:01:33,259
<i>Emilia and Red Dragon's group</i>
<i>are planning a huge meeting.</i>

25
00:01:33,343 --> 00:01:36,095
<i>It could be the perfect chance</i>
<i>to arrest them.</i>

26
00:01:36,179 --> 00:01:38,306
[Julio] <i>The lion is not gonna sleep</i>

27
00:01:38,389 --> 00:01:42,852
<i>until he puts this pesky flock of sheep</i>

28
00:01:42,936 --> 00:01:44,229
<i>down the drain.</i>

29
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:57,242
Hey! Hey! Hey!

30
00:01:58,743 --> 00:02:01,704
Little Red Riding Hood!

31
00:02:03,081 --> 00:02:04,624
Where do you think you're going?

32
00:02:05,375 --> 00:02:08,545
And since when did I have to
ask for your permission, Papa?

33
00:02:09,420 --> 00:02:11,631
I'm asking you properly.

34
00:02:11,714 --> 00:02:13,424
Where are you going?

35
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:15,093
Spare me, Papa, okay?

36
00:02:15,176 --> 00:02:16,803
You're ruining my good mood.

37
00:02:17,345 --> 00:02:18,888
Wherever it is, you're not going.

38
00:02:19,389 --> 00:02:21,933
No, Papa! I know this already.

39
00:02:22,016 --> 00:02:23,977
The lion is envious of the lioness

40
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:26,813
because you know that after that meeting,

41
00:02:26,896 --> 00:02:28,356
I'll become more powerful than you,

42
00:02:28,439 --> 00:02:30,650
and you don't want that. I know that.

43
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:50,295
Enough with your delusions, Emilia.

44
00:02:50,879 --> 00:02:53,047
When I say you can't go,

45
00:02:53,548 --> 00:02:55,758
you can't go.

46
00:02:56,342 --> 00:02:59,304
And you will thank me for this later on,

47
00:02:59,929 --> 00:03:01,806
because believe it or not,

48
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:04,601
I'm doing all this for you.

49
00:03:05,435 --> 00:03:07,645
That's it! I'm done
being your loyal follower.

50
00:03:07,729 --> 00:03:09,105
I'm done being your daughter.

51
00:03:09,188 --> 00:03:11,274
I won't follow your orders anymore.

52
00:03:11,357 --> 00:03:13,318
That's it. So, goodbye.

53
00:03:15,403 --> 00:03:16,738
[gunshots]

54
00:03:17,947 --> 00:03:19,115
[screams]

55
00:03:19,782 --> 00:03:20,909
[Emilia gasps]

56
00:03:22,744 --> 00:03:25,330
[hyperventilates]

57
00:03:31,377 --> 00:03:33,421
[groans]

58
00:03:34,505 --> 00:03:37,759
[groaning]

59
00:03:47,393 --> 00:03:49,896
[shrieks]

60
00:03:51,481 --> 00:03:53,733
[groaning]

61
00:04:01,658 --> 00:04:04,160
[ominous music]

62
00:04:07,497 --> 00:04:09,499
And what was that for, Papa?

63
00:04:10,917 --> 00:04:12,252
Are you trying to kill me?!

64
00:04:13,086 --> 00:04:14,254
Of course not!

65
00:04:14,337 --> 00:04:16,923
I just wanted to get your attention.

66
00:04:17,006 --> 00:04:17,966
I missed, see?

67
00:04:18,049 --> 00:04:20,343
Can you please tell me what's going on?

68
00:04:20,426 --> 00:04:22,011
[tense music playing]

69
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:26,933
That's it. I'm leaving.

70
00:04:27,016 --> 00:04:30,561
[Emilia yelps]
Enough, Papa! You're scaring me!

71
00:04:36,067 --> 00:04:38,069
She's so stubborn!

72
00:04:38,569 --> 00:04:39,570
Magbanua.

73
00:04:40,905 --> 00:04:43,032
Call your men,

74
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:46,411
and tell them that
my stubborn little daughter

75
00:04:46,494 --> 00:04:47,912
is on her way there.

76
00:04:51,916 --> 00:04:54,127
I don't know what I'm going
to do with that woman.

77
00:04:56,838 --> 00:05:00,425
[Arnaldo crying]

78
00:05:00,508 --> 00:05:02,176
[panting]

79
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:03,261
[shouts]

80
00:05:06,264 --> 00:05:07,265
[shrieks]

81
00:05:35,668 --> 00:05:38,171
[ominous music playing]

82
00:05:58,232 --> 00:05:59,358
[groans]

83
00:06:00,526 --> 00:06:03,488
[groaning]

84
00:06:10,328 --> 00:06:13,623
-[ominous music intensifies]
-[Arnaldo hyperventilates]

85
00:06:20,463 --> 00:06:23,674
[Ivy] <i>Mr. Mayor, my name is Ivy.</i>

86
00:06:23,966 --> 00:06:25,635
<i>Ivy Aguas.</i>

87
00:06:29,931 --> 00:06:32,558
[Arnaldo] <i>You really are</i>
<i>something else, Miss Aguas.</i>

88
00:06:32,642 --> 00:06:35,103
[Ivy] <i>I'm sure of my feelings for you.</i>

89
00:06:35,186 --> 00:06:37,105
<i>Arnaldo, I'm not playing you.</i>

90
00:06:37,188 --> 00:06:38,314
<i>I love you.</i>

91
00:06:38,397 --> 00:06:40,274
<i>I love you, Arnaldo.</i>

92
00:06:40,358 --> 00:06:42,318
[Arnaldo] <i>Ivy Aguas, I love you.</i>

93
00:06:42,401 --> 00:06:44,862
<i>-Will you marry me?</i>
<i>-Yes, Arnaldo.</i>

94
00:06:44,946 --> 00:06:47,949
[Nimfa] <i>She's the one feeding</i>
<i>information to Diego's camp.</i>

95
00:06:48,032 --> 00:06:50,243
<i>-That's not true!</i>
<i>-She's Diego's spy!</i>

96
00:06:50,326 --> 00:06:51,285
<i>That's not true!</i>

97
00:06:51,369 --> 00:06:53,412
<i>Mayor, you need to know that Ivy is--</i>

98
00:06:53,496 --> 00:06:54,956
-<i>That's not true!</i>
-[gunshot]

99
00:07:00,962 --> 00:07:02,797
[Arthur] <i>I've got Ivy Aguas.</i>

100
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:04,090
[Arnaldo] <i>Well, I have you!</i>

101
00:07:04,465 --> 00:07:05,508
<i>I can easily kill you</i>

102
00:07:05,591 --> 00:07:08,302
<i>and make it look</i>
<i>like you committed suicide,</i>

103
00:07:08,386 --> 00:07:10,096
<i>just like what I did to Carlotta.</i>

104
00:07:10,179 --> 00:07:12,223
<i>-You monster!</i>
<i>-I didn't mean to!</i>

105
00:07:12,306 --> 00:07:13,891
<i>-You monster!</i>
<i>-But you love me!</i>

106
00:07:13,975 --> 00:07:15,059
<i>I don't love you!</i>

107
00:07:15,143 --> 00:07:16,727
[Ivy] <i>Mom.</i>

108
00:07:16,811 --> 00:07:18,187
[Camia] <i>Lily, dear.</i>

109
00:07:18,896 --> 00:07:21,399
[Arnaldo] <i>Tell me.</i>
<i>You're Lily Cruz, right?</i>

110
00:07:21,482 --> 00:07:22,358
<i>Answer me!</i>

111
00:07:22,442 --> 00:07:25,194
[Lily] <i>Yes! I am!</i>

112
00:07:25,278 --> 00:07:27,238
<i>I am Lily Cruz!</i>

113
00:07:27,655 --> 00:07:29,699
-<i>No!</i>
-[gunshot]

114
00:07:35,079 --> 00:07:36,873
[ethereal music playing]

115
00:07:36,956 --> 00:07:39,459
[Arnaldo] <i>Ivy Aguas.</i>

116
00:07:41,919 --> 00:07:43,921
<i>You were my happiness.</i>

117
00:07:46,382 --> 00:07:49,927
<i>But you also caused my downfall.</i>

118
00:07:53,931 --> 00:07:57,643
[tense music playing]

119
00:08:22,710 --> 00:08:24,921
<i>You killed the old Arnaldo.</i>

120
00:08:27,256 --> 00:08:29,342
<i>But now that my memory is back,</i>

121
00:08:30,885 --> 00:08:33,346
<i>I'll make you pay.</i>

122
00:08:33,429 --> 00:08:35,932
[tense music intensifies]

123
00:08:41,479 --> 00:08:43,689
Yeah. She's already there.

124
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:51,864
Mercedes, who invited you?

125
00:08:51,948 --> 00:08:55,409
Didn't Madam Baby Dragon
already kick you out?

126
00:08:55,576 --> 00:08:58,246
I wasn't kicked out.
I simply went on vacation.

127
00:08:58,788 --> 00:09:00,414
Why, were you two invited?

128
00:09:00,498 --> 00:09:01,582
Of course.

129
00:09:01,958 --> 00:09:04,293
[Mercedes] Well, not anymore.

130
00:09:07,046 --> 00:09:08,589
[tense music playing]

131
00:09:25,481 --> 00:09:27,066
Yes, I'm back.

132
00:09:27,650 --> 00:09:31,404
A bunch of bruises won't keep me
from being at this event.

133
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:34,824
Just make sure you're loyal to Emilia.

134
00:09:35,575 --> 00:09:36,909
Otherwise,

135
00:09:37,618 --> 00:09:39,078
you'll get something worse than that.

136
00:09:40,246 --> 00:09:41,956
[tense music continues]

137
00:10:08,316 --> 00:10:09,400
[Emilia] Come on. Let's move!

138
00:10:09,483 --> 00:10:11,152
I'm in a hurry! Move it!

139
00:10:15,364 --> 00:10:16,532
Drive!

140
00:10:23,998 --> 00:10:26,917
[tense music swelling]

141
00:10:38,179 --> 00:10:40,348
Mr. Ramon Lim of the North.

142
00:10:40,765 --> 00:10:41,766
Welcome, sir.

143
00:10:44,143 --> 00:10:46,145
Mr. Silverio Victoria of the East.

144
00:10:46,854 --> 00:10:47,897
Welcome.

145
00:10:49,231 --> 00:10:51,942
Mr. Carlos Isidro of the West. Welcome.

146
00:10:54,695 --> 00:10:57,490
Mr. Oscar Evangelista
of the South. Welcome.

147
00:11:09,919 --> 00:11:13,798
[tense music intensifies]

148
00:11:26,936 --> 00:11:28,104
-Cheers!
-[glasses clinking]

149
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:34,693
-[laughter, chatter in the background]
-[glasses clinking]

150
00:11:36,487 --> 00:11:38,072
[man] Cheers! Cheers, everyone.

151
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:42,076
[Mercedes] <i>Thank you for gracing</i>
<i>this occasion.</i>

152
00:11:42,159 --> 00:11:43,994
And as a token of our appreciation,

153
00:11:44,078 --> 00:11:47,581
Red Dragon has prepared something
to delight your senses.

154
00:11:47,665 --> 00:11:49,166
-Wow.
-Yes.

155
00:11:58,092 --> 00:11:59,844
-Cheers! Cheers!
-Cheers! Cheers!

156
00:11:59,927 --> 00:12:01,429
-[glasses clinking]
-Yeah!

157
00:12:01,512 --> 00:12:03,931
[man] I like it.
I like it, I like it, I like it!

158
00:12:05,641 --> 00:12:07,852
[man] Very good! I like it!

159
00:12:07,935 --> 00:12:10,354
-Hello.
-How are you?

160
00:12:10,771 --> 00:12:11,981
Very nice!

161
00:12:14,608 --> 00:12:16,068
Beautiful! Beautiful!

162
00:12:26,495 --> 00:12:28,539
[tense music playing]

163
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:42,261
[Magbanua] Governor.

164
00:12:43,179 --> 00:12:45,598
Our men have been notified that
your daughter is on the way.

165
00:12:46,265 --> 00:12:47,266
That's good.

166
00:12:48,767 --> 00:12:52,021
Make sure nothing happens to my daughter.

167
00:12:53,522 --> 00:12:54,356
Yes, sir.

168
00:12:55,274 --> 00:12:56,317
[Magbanua] Let's go.

169
00:12:59,028 --> 00:13:00,029
[exhales]

170
00:13:02,990 --> 00:13:03,991
[man] Beautiful!

171
00:13:05,242 --> 00:13:06,243
Very nice!

172
00:13:14,752 --> 00:13:15,669
Governor.

173
00:13:17,171 --> 00:13:18,631
Yes, that's the one.

174
00:13:20,007 --> 00:13:22,426
-I'll take my leave, sir.
-Okay, thank you.

175
00:13:36,899 --> 00:13:38,567
[men laughing]

176
00:13:38,651 --> 00:13:39,652
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

177
00:13:39,735 --> 00:13:41,028
Cheers!

178
00:13:41,111 --> 00:13:42,112
[glasses clinking]

179
00:13:43,322 --> 00:13:44,907
[indistinct chatter]

180
00:13:45,366 --> 00:13:47,076
[upbeat music playing]

181
00:13:59,922 --> 00:14:01,048
Yes.

182
00:14:01,423 --> 00:14:03,092
[tense music playing]

183
00:14:13,936 --> 00:14:16,480
[phone buzzing]

184
00:14:17,481 --> 00:14:18,691
Lily, it's me, Diego.

185
00:14:18,774 --> 00:14:20,401
Diego, we're here.

186
00:14:20,484 --> 00:14:21,902
Don't come in yet.

187
00:14:22,403 --> 00:14:23,571
Something doesn't feel right.

188
00:14:24,113 --> 00:14:25,614
We're already here, Diego.

189
00:14:25,698 --> 00:14:27,157
<i>If your suspicions are correct…</i>

190
00:14:27,241 --> 00:14:29,326
then we shouldn't waste any more time!

191
00:14:29,410 --> 00:14:30,703
Are they all there?

192
00:14:31,537 --> 00:14:32,872
Emilia's still not here.

193
00:14:32,955 --> 00:14:34,331
Why isn't she there yet?

194
00:14:42,423 --> 00:14:45,217
[suspenseful music swelling]

195
00:15:00,608 --> 00:15:02,318
[Julio] It's been a while.

196
00:15:07,656 --> 00:15:11,619
[classical music playing]

197
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:17,875
-[man] Waiter.
-Sweet.

198
00:15:41,106 --> 00:15:43,067
This must be what they call

199
00:15:43,150 --> 00:15:46,236
the nectar of the gods from Mount Olympus.

200
00:15:48,656 --> 00:15:49,657
Cheers.

201
00:15:49,990 --> 00:15:52,534
[music continues]

202
00:15:55,162 --> 00:15:57,539
[gunshots]

203
00:15:57,623 --> 00:16:00,042
[Emilia screams]
What was that? Go check it out!

204
00:16:01,919 --> 00:16:03,170
[gunshots]

205
00:16:04,922 --> 00:16:09,468
[classical music swells]

206
00:16:13,931 --> 00:16:16,058
-[gunshots]
-[classical music playing]

207
00:16:19,395 --> 00:16:22,064
[gunfire continue]

208
00:16:22,147 --> 00:16:23,148
Diego?

209
00:16:23,524 --> 00:16:25,234
-Let's go.
-Move! Move!

210
00:16:27,069 --> 00:16:28,529
[gunshots]

211
00:16:28,904 --> 00:16:31,907
[classical music continues]

212
00:16:45,796 --> 00:16:49,341
[rapid gunfire]

213
00:16:57,975 --> 00:17:00,644
[music continues]

214
00:17:02,438 --> 00:17:06,108
[gunfire continues over classical music]

215
00:17:38,932 --> 00:17:40,350
[classical music fades]

216
00:17:40,434 --> 00:17:42,102
So, this…

217
00:17:43,395 --> 00:17:47,149
is what victory tastes like.

218
00:17:49,234 --> 00:17:50,486
[Julio] <i>Soft.</i>

219
00:17:52,029 --> 00:17:53,113
<i>Mellow.</i>

220
00:17:55,115 --> 00:17:57,993
<i>Full-bodied and warm.</i>

221
00:18:00,245 --> 00:18:02,081
<i>I can't go wrong.</i>

222
00:18:07,669 --> 00:18:09,129
Cheers to life.

223
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:12,049
My life.

224
00:18:12,508 --> 00:18:15,177
[tense music intensifies]

225
00:18:17,137 --> 00:18:19,389
-[gunshots]
-[Emilia screams]

226
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:21,975
[groans]

227
00:18:28,482 --> 00:18:31,068
[gunshots]

228
00:18:33,946 --> 00:18:36,323
-[gunfire continues]
-[tense music intensifies]

229
00:18:48,669 --> 00:18:49,670
-[gunshot]
-[yelps]

230
00:18:54,299 --> 00:18:55,509
[Jaguar] Let's go, Emilia!

231
00:19:08,230 --> 00:19:09,398
Lily, let's go!

232
00:19:09,481 --> 00:19:11,775
What are you talking about?!
Can't you see?!

233
00:19:11,859 --> 00:19:13,694
This is a massacre, Agent Salonga!

234
00:19:13,777 --> 00:19:15,195
My men are already in position!

235
00:19:15,279 --> 00:19:17,156
It's important for us
to keep you safe! Let's go!

236
00:19:17,239 --> 00:19:21,577
If the Big Four die, who will
testify against Red Dragon?!

237
00:19:22,161 --> 00:19:24,580
[gunshots]

238
00:19:26,206 --> 00:19:28,208
Come on, let's go! Let's go!

239
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:29,668
[gunshots]

240
00:19:33,213 --> 00:19:34,256
Mercedes.

241
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:37,926
[gunshots]

242
00:19:42,598 --> 00:19:43,432
Get up! Come on!

243
00:20:02,951 --> 00:20:03,952
[gunshots]

244
00:20:04,661 --> 00:20:05,704
Let's go.

245
00:20:06,121 --> 00:20:08,540
-Come with me.
-I won't go with you.

246
00:20:08,624 --> 00:20:11,001
If you don't come with me,
you'll die here!

247
00:20:11,501 --> 00:20:13,128
[action music playing]

248
00:20:22,512 --> 00:20:25,974
[suspenseful music swelling]

249
00:20:48,121 --> 00:20:49,289
[knocking on door]

250
00:20:49,957 --> 00:20:51,083
Come in!

251
00:20:51,875 --> 00:20:54,294
Ma'am, something bad happened
to Boss Oscar.

252
00:20:55,003 --> 00:20:56,004
What do you mean?

253
00:20:56,380 --> 00:20:58,882
Boss Oscar died along with the
other members of the Big Four!

254
00:20:59,508 --> 00:21:01,927
What? My Oscar is dead?

255
00:21:02,386 --> 00:21:03,262
Yes, ma'am!

256
00:21:03,345 --> 00:21:05,138
That's why we need to hide and lie low.

257
00:21:05,222 --> 00:21:07,266
They might come for us next.

258
00:21:07,849 --> 00:21:09,268
This can't be.

259
00:21:11,144 --> 00:21:12,229
No.

260
00:21:13,355 --> 00:21:14,356
No.

261
00:21:15,607 --> 00:21:17,526
We will not hide.

262
00:21:18,235 --> 00:21:22,698
I'll make sure that his business
continues to thrive.

263
00:21:23,073 --> 00:21:24,491
He put this up.

264
00:21:25,367 --> 00:21:28,412
And I know that he wants me to continue.

265
00:21:29,162 --> 00:21:30,789
All operations will continue.

266
00:21:31,415 --> 00:21:33,458
Now, tell everyone…

267
00:21:33,875 --> 00:21:36,670
that I will be taking over the business.

268
00:21:41,383 --> 00:21:43,176
Do you have a problem with that?

269
00:21:43,802 --> 00:21:44,886
Do you?

270
00:21:46,972 --> 00:21:51,268
I think you're forgetting
that Oscar ordered you

271
00:21:51,351 --> 00:21:54,938
to do everything I say.

272
00:21:57,065 --> 00:21:58,358
Just so you know,

273
00:21:58,442 --> 00:22:04,114
I hold all the transaction
records of this business.

274
00:22:04,656 --> 00:22:05,657
Hmm?

275
00:22:06,074 --> 00:22:08,076
Yes, ma'am. We're aware of that.

276
00:22:09,995 --> 00:22:10,996
Good.

277
00:22:12,247 --> 00:22:15,751
Now, go and tell everyone who's boss.

278
00:22:17,085 --> 00:22:18,545
While I'll be grieving…

279
00:22:20,505 --> 00:22:22,090
for my Oscar.

280
00:22:24,343 --> 00:22:25,635
[cries]

281
00:22:30,974 --> 00:22:33,518
Go! Just go and leave me!

282
00:22:35,520 --> 00:22:36,438
[door opens]

283
00:22:39,232 --> 00:22:40,233
[door closes]

284
00:22:45,238 --> 00:22:46,490
Daddy.

285
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:49,201
[exhales]

286
00:22:51,369 --> 00:22:53,830
That was so fast, Daddy.

287
00:22:55,665 --> 00:22:57,876
[laughs]

288
00:22:59,961 --> 00:23:01,505
That's it?

289
00:23:01,588 --> 00:23:04,466
[laughs]

290
00:23:08,345 --> 00:23:09,930
Well, Natalie…

291
00:23:11,264 --> 00:23:15,102
I guess I need to propose a toast

292
00:23:16,478 --> 00:23:18,647
to me.

293
00:23:20,357 --> 00:23:22,192
Cheers, Natalie.

294
00:23:22,275 --> 00:23:24,277
[laughs]

295
00:23:25,153 --> 00:23:26,988
<i>Four syndicate bosses,</i>
<i>known as The Big Four,</i>

296
00:23:27,072 --> 00:23:28,323
<i>were recently massacred.</i>

297
00:23:28,406 --> 00:23:31,076
<i>They were identified as Oscar</i>
<i>Evangelista, Carlos Isidro,</i>

298
00:23:31,159 --> 00:23:33,703
<i>Silverio Victoria, and Ramon Lim.</i>

299
00:23:33,787 --> 00:23:36,414
<i>They were known to be associates</i>
<i>of the most powerful crime lord</i>

300
00:23:36,498 --> 00:23:39,042
<i>in the country, known as Red Dragon,</i>

301
00:23:39,126 --> 00:23:41,670
<i>who was recently identified</i>
<i>as Helena Montoya.</i>

302
00:23:41,753 --> 00:23:45,966
<i>Authorities have been unable</i>
<i>to locate her until now.</i>

303
00:23:46,049 --> 00:23:47,551
<i>So, where is Red Dragon?</i>

304
00:23:47,634 --> 00:23:50,095
<i>Who is behind the massacre of her allies?</i>

305
00:23:50,178 --> 00:23:52,806
[laughs]

306
00:23:52,889 --> 00:23:54,891
[reporter] <i>Stay tuned for more updates.</i>

307
00:23:54,975 --> 00:23:56,560
<i>This is Willie Gabon, reporting.</i>

308
00:24:01,189 --> 00:24:02,399
-[shouts]
-[phone clatters]

309
00:24:04,359 --> 00:24:07,821
-[shouting]
-[thumping]

310
00:24:13,076 --> 00:24:15,245
[Julio] <i>Who could the mastermind be?</i>

311
00:24:15,328 --> 00:24:17,873
[laughs]

312
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:30,552
[claps]

313
00:24:32,345 --> 00:24:33,513
[sighs contently]

314
00:24:39,769 --> 00:24:43,273
Ouch! Hey, be careful! It hurts!

315
00:24:43,773 --> 00:24:46,026
I'm sorry. But I'm done anyway.

316
00:24:46,693 --> 00:24:47,694
Wait.

317
00:24:48,111 --> 00:24:50,739
How did you know
that my life was in danger?

318
00:24:53,700 --> 00:24:55,327
Didn't I tell you that…

319
00:24:56,369 --> 00:24:58,079
I'd always keep an eye on you?

320
00:24:59,039 --> 00:25:01,124
Wait, did you install a
CCTV camera in my house?

321
00:25:01,208 --> 00:25:03,126
Or did you ask someone to spy on me?

322
00:25:03,210 --> 00:25:04,252
No.

323
00:25:05,921 --> 00:25:10,133
I've already told you that
I will watch your every move…

324
00:25:11,259 --> 00:25:13,053
and that I'll protect you.

325
00:25:13,678 --> 00:25:16,431
So, can you please stop
asking so many questions?

326
00:25:17,265 --> 00:25:18,266
Hmm.

327
00:25:18,934 --> 00:25:22,395
Wait. Jaguar, do you have any idea

328
00:25:22,479 --> 00:25:25,106
who could be behind the bloodbath earlier?

329
00:25:28,401 --> 00:25:29,694
I'll find out eventually.

330
00:25:30,403 --> 00:25:33,031
You know, I have a feeling it's Mercedes.

331
00:25:33,114 --> 00:25:36,284
Because Mercedes knew I was
getting along with the Big Four.

332
00:25:36,368 --> 00:25:38,870
And she wants to take my position, right?

333
00:25:38,954 --> 00:25:40,622
So, she's the mastermind!

334
00:25:40,705 --> 00:25:42,374
I can bet my life on that.

335
00:25:44,334 --> 00:25:45,585
That's impossible.

336
00:25:45,669 --> 00:25:48,296
You mentioned that she was
at the meeting earlier.

337
00:25:50,382 --> 00:25:52,509
She couldn't have been the mastermind.

338
00:25:53,134 --> 00:25:54,135
You have a point.

339
00:25:54,678 --> 00:25:56,972
Um, I think it's Lily Cruz.
It's Lily Cruz.

340
00:25:57,055 --> 00:25:59,516
I can bet my life on it
for the second time.

341
00:25:59,599 --> 00:26:00,892
She's the mastermind.

342
00:26:02,102 --> 00:26:03,728
She'd never do that, Emilia.

343
00:26:04,354 --> 00:26:06,231
She's incapable of killing people.

344
00:26:06,898 --> 00:26:08,233
Oh, please, Jaguar!

345
00:26:08,316 --> 00:26:10,193
Can you please stop antagonizing me?

346
00:26:10,277 --> 00:26:11,778
And just support me, okay?

347
00:26:12,988 --> 00:26:15,991
Emilia, I'm merely stating facts.

348
00:26:17,325 --> 00:26:19,619
Shush. Just support me, okay?

349
00:26:36,511 --> 00:26:38,972
[ominous music playing]

350
00:26:45,645 --> 00:26:46,688
Arnaldo?

351
00:26:47,647 --> 00:26:49,524
What happened to you? Are you okay?!

352
00:26:51,651 --> 00:26:53,361
Come on, I'll take you to the hospital.

353
00:26:53,445 --> 00:26:54,362
No.

354
00:27:01,411 --> 00:27:02,662
I'm fine.

355
00:27:05,582 --> 00:27:07,000
Thank you for your concern.

356
00:27:08,084 --> 00:27:09,252
Are you sure?

357
00:27:11,129 --> 00:27:11,963
Bless you.

358
00:27:17,927 --> 00:27:19,304
Okay. I'll leave now.

359
00:27:19,387 --> 00:27:21,181
I just came back for these books.

360
00:27:22,265 --> 00:27:23,266
Take care.

361
00:27:35,820 --> 00:27:38,365
[ominous music intensifies]

362
00:27:50,794 --> 00:27:52,796
<i>-Good morning, friend.</i>
<i>-"Friend"?!</i>

363
00:27:52,879 --> 00:27:54,881
<i>-You're a murderer!</i>
<i>-Wait! Hold on!</i>

364
00:27:54,964 --> 00:27:56,299
[Arnaldo] <i>You seem to know who I am.</i>

365
00:27:56,383 --> 00:27:58,843
<i>-You're Arnaldo Ardiente.</i>
<i>-Good for you.</i>

366
00:27:58,927 --> 00:28:00,345
<i>I don't even know who I am.</i>

367
00:28:00,428 --> 00:28:03,139
<i>-Peace be with you.</i>
<i>-Just drop the act, will you?!</i>

368
00:28:03,223 --> 00:28:04,808
<i>-Jepoy, stop it.</i>
<i>-Anna!</i>

369
00:28:04,891 --> 00:28:06,351
<i>Don't defend that bastard!</i>

370
00:28:06,434 --> 00:28:07,519
<i>He'll kill you!</i>

371
00:28:07,602 --> 00:28:10,188
<i>But he wasn't fighting back, right?</i>

372
00:28:10,271 --> 00:28:13,942
<i>Have you ever thought</i>
<i>of returning to your family?</i>

373
00:28:14,025 --> 00:28:16,444
<i>I know why you're asking me this.</i>

374
00:28:18,071 --> 00:28:20,365
<i>You're making sure I've really changed.</i>

375
00:28:20,448 --> 00:28:21,491
<i>What are you hiding from me?</i>

376
00:28:21,574 --> 00:28:24,369
<i>Why don't you just forget</i>
<i>about everything, Arnaldo?!</i>

377
00:28:24,452 --> 00:28:27,372
<i>This is your chance to start over.</i>

378
00:28:38,007 --> 00:28:39,175
Anna.

379
00:28:47,934 --> 00:28:49,144
Where are you going?

380
00:28:49,894 --> 00:28:51,062
None of your business.

381
00:28:51,730 --> 00:28:54,357
You're still rude to me
after I saved your life?

382
00:28:54,899 --> 00:28:58,570
I didn't ask you to do that,
so I don't owe you anything.

383
00:28:59,487 --> 00:29:00,655
But, you know what?

384
00:29:01,030 --> 00:29:03,158
Just so we can settle this,
how much do you want?

385
00:29:03,241 --> 00:29:04,534
I'll pay you.

386
00:29:05,243 --> 00:29:07,412
[tense music]

387
00:29:08,955 --> 00:29:12,250
You think I need your dirty money?

388
00:29:13,084 --> 00:29:14,919
You can keep it, Mercedes.

389
00:29:16,504 --> 00:29:17,422
[sighs]

390
00:29:17,505 --> 00:29:20,383
But I want you to know I can
help you take Red Dragon down.

391
00:29:20,467 --> 00:29:21,676
[scoffs]

392
00:29:21,926 --> 00:29:23,970
Leave me out of your crazy schemes.

393
00:29:24,929 --> 00:29:26,389
I'm not crazy.

394
00:29:27,348 --> 00:29:29,350
You only got shot on the shoulder, right?

395
00:29:29,934 --> 00:29:31,728
Then why do you sound
like you have brain damage?

396
00:29:33,188 --> 00:29:36,149
For your information,
Red Dragon wants you dead.

397
00:29:36,232 --> 00:29:38,443
She wants all of you dead.

398
00:29:38,860 --> 00:29:40,695
-That's not true!
-It is.

399
00:29:40,779 --> 00:29:42,405
Don't be stupid, Mercedes.

400
00:29:42,489 --> 00:29:45,283
In times like these,
you can't afford to be stupid.

401
00:29:45,909 --> 00:29:47,368
And in case you didn't know,

402
00:29:47,952 --> 00:29:50,997
she had the Big Four killed

403
00:29:51,080 --> 00:29:54,167
so she could hold on to all the power.

404
00:29:54,250 --> 00:29:57,170
If she could do that to her partners,

405
00:29:57,253 --> 00:30:00,048
what more to a mere lackey like you?

406
00:30:00,131 --> 00:30:01,257
No.

407
00:30:01,966 --> 00:30:03,259
I trust Red Dragon.

408
00:30:03,760 --> 00:30:06,721
And no matter what you say,
I will never side with you.

409
00:30:06,805 --> 00:30:09,474
I would rather die than turn
my back on Red Dragon--

410
00:30:09,557 --> 00:30:11,893
You're siding with the devil!

411
00:30:12,852 --> 00:30:15,063
I'd rather do that than work with you.

412
00:30:17,982 --> 00:30:19,734
Remember, Mercedes.

413
00:30:20,068 --> 00:30:23,321
You need me more than I need you.

414
00:30:24,906 --> 00:30:27,116
If you've made up your mind, then fine.

415
00:30:28,660 --> 00:30:33,706
I just hope you don't regret
the stupid choice you made.

416
00:30:38,419 --> 00:30:39,420
[door opens]

417
00:30:40,547 --> 00:30:41,464
[door closes]

418
00:30:41,548 --> 00:30:43,633
[tense music swelling]

419
00:30:49,389 --> 00:30:50,390
[birds chirping]

420
00:30:53,601 --> 00:30:54,602
Emilia!

421
00:30:55,144 --> 00:30:56,938
Emilia, come here.

422
00:30:57,730 --> 00:30:59,691
Join me for breakfast.

423
00:30:59,774 --> 00:31:02,151
-Good morning, Papa.
-Good morning. Good morning.

424
00:31:02,235 --> 00:31:03,236
Come on.

425
00:31:04,237 --> 00:31:05,238
Um…

426
00:31:05,738 --> 00:31:08,283
What seems to be wrong with your arm?

427
00:31:09,075 --> 00:31:11,578
-Nothing's wrong, Papa.
-Oh, nothing? Really?

428
00:31:11,661 --> 00:31:12,954
-What if I do this?
-[Emilia screams]

429
00:31:13,037 --> 00:31:14,747
-Papa!
-See?

430
00:31:14,831 --> 00:31:17,250
You flinched even before I hit you.

431
00:31:18,251 --> 00:31:19,836
That just proves my point.

432
00:31:21,296 --> 00:31:22,922
You went to the meeting, didn't you?

433
00:31:23,631 --> 00:31:26,259
I have an obligation
to Mama's organization.

434
00:31:26,342 --> 00:31:27,468
[Julio sighs]

435
00:31:27,844 --> 00:31:31,681
This is what happens
when you don't listen to me.

436
00:31:32,015 --> 00:31:36,436
I told you to just stay home
and not go there.

437
00:31:36,519 --> 00:31:39,647
But you were so stubborn.
See what happened?

438
00:31:40,064 --> 00:31:42,233
Were you behind the attack, Papa?

439
00:31:43,526 --> 00:31:45,653
Oh, come on, Emilia.

440
00:31:46,446 --> 00:31:50,033
Are you seriously accusing me of
doing something wrong or evil?

441
00:31:50,491 --> 00:31:52,493
-Don't be silly.
-Oh, come on, Papa.

442
00:31:52,577 --> 00:31:54,829
You wanted me to stay home.

443
00:31:54,913 --> 00:31:56,456
How did you know what would happen?

444
00:31:56,539 --> 00:31:58,374
I wasn't insisting on anything.

445
00:31:58,917 --> 00:31:59,918
Look.

446
00:32:00,335 --> 00:32:03,504
This is what happens
to criminal organizations

447
00:32:03,588 --> 00:32:05,632
when a power struggle occurs.

448
00:32:06,215 --> 00:32:09,427
In the end, the members
go against each other,

449
00:32:09,510 --> 00:32:12,013
to the point where they end up
killing one another.

450
00:32:12,096 --> 00:32:14,974
You see, I've seen this over and over

451
00:32:15,058 --> 00:32:17,268
and over and over again.

452
00:32:17,852 --> 00:32:20,188
That's why there's nothing
special about me

453
00:32:20,271 --> 00:32:23,066
knowing or sensing
something bad would happen.

454
00:32:23,650 --> 00:32:28,237
Pure and simple common sense.

455
00:32:28,321 --> 00:32:29,989
And that's your problem.

456
00:32:30,657 --> 00:32:34,869
You always lead with your heart,
and not with your head.

457
00:32:36,579 --> 00:32:38,706
Good grief, Emilia.

458
00:32:39,332 --> 00:32:43,211
You should use your head
every now and then.

459
00:32:43,294 --> 00:32:45,338
I mean, you have common sense.

460
00:32:45,964 --> 00:32:48,216
You just choose not to use it.

461
00:32:48,299 --> 00:32:50,009
[tense music playing]

462
00:33:26,295 --> 00:33:27,296
Have some water.

463
00:33:34,554 --> 00:33:37,181
Did you hear about what happened
to the Big Four?

464
00:33:39,100 --> 00:33:40,101
Big Four?

465
00:33:42,478 --> 00:33:45,064
I called Lily up.
She says she's all right.

466
00:33:45,815 --> 00:33:47,608
But we need to be on high alert.

467
00:33:47,692 --> 00:33:50,653
They might end up needing our help.

468
00:33:54,365 --> 00:33:56,451
I'm glad you're talking to me again.

469
00:33:58,911 --> 00:34:00,371
I'm just being careful, Anna.

470
00:34:01,247 --> 00:34:03,249
I don't want to upset you again.

471
00:34:29,108 --> 00:34:32,028
[Jepoy's phone ringing]

472
00:34:36,949 --> 00:34:38,576
[line ringing]

473
00:34:57,678 --> 00:34:59,097
[quietly] I want you.

474
00:35:31,712 --> 00:35:34,465
[Jepoy's phone rings]

475
00:35:45,977 --> 00:35:47,311
Hey, lover boy.

476
00:35:48,896 --> 00:35:49,730
[Natalie] <i>So…</i>

477
00:35:50,481 --> 00:35:52,400
I've been a bad girl.

478
00:35:53,151 --> 00:35:55,153
Are you going to punish me?

479
00:35:56,195 --> 00:35:57,446
Hmm?

480
00:35:57,530 --> 00:35:59,615
[tense music playing]

481
00:36:08,374 --> 00:36:09,917
That was weird.

482
00:36:30,104 --> 00:36:32,732
-What are you doing?
-Miss Mercedes.

483
00:36:33,691 --> 00:36:35,026
We thought you were dead.

484
00:36:35,109 --> 00:36:36,360
Who told you that?

485
00:36:36,444 --> 00:36:37,445
Ma'am Emilia did.

486
00:36:37,528 --> 00:36:40,781
She also told us to clean
because she was about to arrive.

487
00:36:41,657 --> 00:36:45,119
You are high-level assassins,
not that woman's maids!

488
00:36:47,413 --> 00:36:48,998
-[door opens]
-[Emilia clears throat]

489
00:36:49,540 --> 00:36:50,708
Wow!

490
00:36:53,044 --> 00:36:55,171
Look who's back!

491
00:36:55,254 --> 00:36:56,672
Back from the dead…

492
00:36:57,965 --> 00:36:59,508
with that look.

493
00:37:00,343 --> 00:37:01,427
Aww.

494
00:37:02,845 --> 00:37:04,847
Don't tell me you're indestructible too?

495
00:37:04,931 --> 00:37:06,599
You don't have any originality.

496
00:37:06,682 --> 00:37:08,851
[tense music playing]

497
00:37:08,935 --> 00:37:10,686
[Emilia grunts]

498
00:37:10,770 --> 00:37:13,814
I've been wanting to do this
for a long time.

499
00:37:13,898 --> 00:37:16,651
But I kept my cool because of Red Dragon.

500
00:37:17,109 --> 00:37:19,737
But now, I've had enough of your attitude.

501
00:37:19,820 --> 00:37:20,947
[Emilia groaning]

502
00:37:21,572 --> 00:37:23,115
[Mercedes grunts, pants]

503
00:37:23,199 --> 00:37:24,700
You silly witch!

504
00:37:24,784 --> 00:37:28,496
You crumpled my expensive silk top!

505
00:37:47,932 --> 00:37:48,891
What's with that look?

506
00:37:50,351 --> 00:37:51,894
-Hey!
-Ask your girlfriend.

507
00:37:51,978 --> 00:37:53,187
What are you talking about?

508
00:37:53,271 --> 00:37:54,272
[phone clatters]

509
00:37:54,647 --> 00:37:55,648
Huh?

510
00:37:59,151 --> 00:38:00,528
Is this how you really see me?

511
00:38:01,612 --> 00:38:03,614
Do you really think I'm this low, Anna?

512
00:38:03,698 --> 00:38:04,740
Yes!

513
00:38:05,658 --> 00:38:07,702
Because I can't give you what you want.

514
00:38:08,119 --> 00:38:10,746
I can't satisfy your desires!

515
00:38:10,830 --> 00:38:12,999
You're right! I do have needs!

516
00:38:16,877 --> 00:38:18,963
But I'm willing to wait
for the day you'll be ready.

517
00:38:20,715 --> 00:38:22,633
Because I love you, Anna.
I love you so much.

518
00:38:22,717 --> 00:38:23,926
You're the only one for me!

519
00:38:28,681 --> 00:38:31,142
There's no one else. Just you.

520
00:38:47,992 --> 00:38:50,536
[Mercedes and Emilia grunt]

521
00:38:50,619 --> 00:38:52,580
Restrain that skinny twig!

522
00:38:52,663 --> 00:38:54,040
[tense music]

523
00:38:54,123 --> 00:38:55,666
I knew it, Mercedes.

524
00:38:55,750 --> 00:38:57,501
From the moment I first saw you,

525
00:38:57,585 --> 00:39:00,421
I knew you wanted to steal my crown!

526
00:39:00,504 --> 00:39:03,132
I don't care about you
and your mother's crown!

527
00:39:03,215 --> 00:39:05,426
All I care about is our survival!

528
00:39:05,509 --> 00:39:07,887
Survival? With that look? Come on!

529
00:39:07,970 --> 00:39:09,972
Stop acting like you're a superhero!

530
00:39:10,056 --> 00:39:11,432
You are so clueless!

531
00:39:11,515 --> 00:39:14,935
The Big Four's men will blame us
for what happened!

532
00:39:15,019 --> 00:39:16,812
They'll get back at us!

533
00:39:16,896 --> 00:39:18,814
You just put everyone's lives at risk!

534
00:39:18,898 --> 00:39:20,399
That's just your opinion!

535
00:39:20,483 --> 00:39:22,234
That is a fact!

536
00:39:22,902 --> 00:39:24,904
And I am the only one who can stop them.

537
00:39:25,988 --> 00:39:28,866
That's why I am taking over
as leader of this group.

538
00:39:28,949 --> 00:39:31,827
[laughs]

539
00:39:34,663 --> 00:39:35,873
Leader?

540
00:39:36,624 --> 00:39:38,501
Leader of this group?

541
00:39:38,584 --> 00:39:40,378
Did I just hear you say that, huh?

542
00:39:40,461 --> 00:39:41,712
That you're the leader of this group?

543
00:39:41,796 --> 00:39:43,172
And how can that be,

544
00:39:43,255 --> 00:39:45,466
when I am the queen
and leader of this group?

545
00:39:46,675 --> 00:39:47,676
Idiot!

546
00:39:55,059 --> 00:39:59,939
Now, I am giving you
five seconds to side with me.

547
00:40:00,689 --> 00:40:01,524
[Emilia] Five!

548
00:40:01,607 --> 00:40:03,692
[Mercedes] Don't waste your
breath counting.

549
00:40:03,776 --> 00:40:04,568
Four!

550
00:40:04,652 --> 00:40:07,238
Because they know who to trust.

551
00:40:07,321 --> 00:40:08,406
Three!

552
00:40:08,489 --> 00:40:11,409
Just accept that you're
completely powerless!

553
00:40:11,492 --> 00:40:13,077
-Two!
-Just like--

554
00:40:13,327 --> 00:40:14,370
[woman] One.

555
00:40:14,662 --> 00:40:17,123
[suspenseful music]

556
00:40:21,293 --> 00:40:22,420
Red Dragon?

557
00:40:23,921 --> 00:40:24,964
Mama!

558
00:40:25,381 --> 00:40:27,049
I'm sorry, Mercedes.

559
00:40:27,425 --> 00:40:30,261
I seem to have cut you off.
Were you saying something?

560
00:40:30,344 --> 00:40:31,887
-[Emilia giggles]
-Hello, darling.

561
00:40:32,680 --> 00:40:33,681
[Emilia chuckles]

562
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:36,684
Never mind.

563
00:40:38,144 --> 00:40:42,022
Time is of the essence here,
and every second counts.

564
00:40:43,149 --> 00:40:48,946
Get everyone here because
I already know who betrayed me.

565
00:40:57,955 --> 00:40:59,039
Mercedes!

566
00:41:00,207 --> 00:41:01,250
Yes, Madam.

567
00:41:08,632 --> 00:41:09,717
Bye!

568
00:41:13,179 --> 00:41:15,055
Let's play a little game.

569
00:41:23,397 --> 00:41:25,941
Who do you suspect
was behind the massacre?

570
00:41:27,651 --> 00:41:30,696
Right now, all we have
are persons of interest.

571
00:41:31,280 --> 00:41:33,574
I'm here because we've received intel

572
00:41:33,657 --> 00:41:35,493
confirming Red Dragon's location.

573
00:41:36,076 --> 00:41:37,495
Did you find her?

574
00:41:39,497 --> 00:41:40,498
Um…

575
00:41:42,875 --> 00:41:45,753
Based on our intel, she's in Macau.

576
00:41:46,212 --> 00:41:47,588
But she's always on the move,

577
00:41:47,671 --> 00:41:50,883
so we really couldn't pinpoint
her exact location.

578
00:41:51,675 --> 00:41:55,221
Agent Salonga, four of
Red Dragon's leaders got killed.

579
00:41:55,888 --> 00:42:00,601
Do you think she would just
let her organization crumble?

580
00:42:00,684 --> 00:42:02,937
-What do you mean?
-It's simple.

581
00:42:03,020 --> 00:42:06,482
Red Dragon's not in Macau.
She's here in the Philippines

582
00:42:06,565 --> 00:42:08,901
to tend to her organization.

583
00:42:09,944 --> 00:42:10,986
It's that simple.

584
00:42:11,570 --> 00:42:13,864
You can't find her in Macau,

585
00:42:13,948 --> 00:42:16,116
because she's here in the Philippines.

586
00:42:29,129 --> 00:42:30,631
[phone rings]

587
00:42:36,637 --> 00:42:37,429
Mercedes?

588
00:42:37,513 --> 00:42:39,807
Drop whatever you're doing,

589
00:42:39,890 --> 00:42:41,559
and come here.

590
00:42:42,059 --> 00:42:42,935
Why?

591
00:42:43,018 --> 00:42:44,770
You'll know when you get here.

592
00:42:44,853 --> 00:42:46,480
[tense music swelling]

593
00:42:51,860 --> 00:42:55,239
LILY, I'M ON MY WAY.

594
00:42:56,949 --> 00:42:59,410
WAIT FOR ME.

595
00:43:04,331 --> 00:43:07,001
[mellow music playing]

596
00:43:30,858 --> 00:43:33,611
I LOVE ANNA.

597
00:43:37,156 --> 00:43:38,699
<i>He really loves me.</i>

598
00:43:55,090 --> 00:43:56,675
Why do you have my phone?

599
00:43:59,678 --> 00:44:00,888
Give me that!

600
00:44:03,098 --> 00:44:04,850
You'll think the worst of me again.

601
00:44:27,956 --> 00:44:28,957
Lily.

602
00:44:29,041 --> 00:44:30,167
Diego.

603
00:44:31,085 --> 00:44:32,753
Red Dragon is back.

604
00:44:34,797 --> 00:44:37,091
So that's why Mercedes
wants all of us there.

605
00:44:38,467 --> 00:44:40,969
Please, don't go back there.

606
00:44:42,846 --> 00:44:44,098
Please, Diego.

607
00:44:44,932 --> 00:44:47,893
Lily, there's no turning back now.

608
00:44:48,519 --> 00:44:51,688
We're so close to taking Red Dragon down.

609
00:44:54,108 --> 00:44:56,110
Then you better take this.

610
00:44:56,193 --> 00:44:58,153
Keep this with you at all times.

611
00:45:00,572 --> 00:45:01,657
What's this?

612
00:45:02,366 --> 00:45:03,659
A tracking device.

613
00:45:03,951 --> 00:45:05,661
So we always know where you are.

614
00:45:20,175 --> 00:45:23,595
[Diego] <i>This could be our last chance</i>
<i>to take Red Dragon down.</i>

615
00:45:23,679 --> 00:45:25,139
<i>She has a huge transaction coming up.</i>

616
00:45:25,222 --> 00:45:26,348
<i>We have to catch her.</i>

617
00:45:26,432 --> 00:45:30,102
[Lily] <i>Just tell me the time,</i>
<i>date, and place,</i>

618
00:45:30,185 --> 00:45:32,104
<i>so we can finally</i>
<i>put a muzzle over her mouth.</i>

619
00:45:32,187 --> 00:45:36,567
[Helena] <i>All of you have</i>
<i>a reason to betray me.</i>

620
00:45:36,650 --> 00:45:39,695
[Emilia] <i>Eeny, meeny, miny, moe.</i>

621
00:45:39,778 --> 00:45:40,946
<i>Moe, moe!</i>

622
00:45:41,029 --> 00:45:42,156
[gunshot]

623
00:45:45,576 --> 00:45:47,494
[Julio] <i>You truly are back.</i>

624
00:45:47,578 --> 00:45:48,912
<i>I love this!</i>

625
00:45:49,621 --> 00:45:51,498
<i>My grandson is back!</i>

626
00:45:51,582 --> 00:45:52,833
[Arnaldo] <i>Cheers.</i>

627
00:45:52,916 --> 00:45:55,419
[theme music playing]
